{%- doc -%}
  SYPerformance badge.

  Only SY's own designs get the accent colour. That distinction is the point of
  the badge system, so do not reuse `in-house` for anything else.

  NOTE ON THE VARIANT NAME: the CSS class stays `in-house` for continuity, but
  the LABEL must not claim manufacturing. SY designs these parts and owns the
  drawings; outside shops cut them. "Made in-house" was wrong and was removed
  2026-08-26.

  @param {string} label - Badge text. Rendered uppercase by CSS.
  @param {string} [variant] - in-house | built-to-order | in-stock | sold-out | sale

  @example
  {% render 'syp-badge', label: 'SYP design', variant: 'in-house' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign badge_classes = 'syp-badge'
  if variant != blank
    assign badge_classes = badge_classes | append: ' syp-badge--' | append: variant
  endif
-%}

<span class="{{ badge_classes }}">{{ label }}</span>
